{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4c1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d4c8-c91a-7382-bd41-b29e82ff449b"},"sequence":187,"recorded_at":1780531400000369,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"297f9a28-ff2a-4f3d-8e2c-f78b2b2814d6","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"297f9a28-ff2a-4f3d-8e2c-f78b2b2814d6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"297f9a28-ff2a-4f3d-8e2c-f78b2b2814d6"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0d4c9-6afb-7711-a7b2-40459769110d"},"task_id":"01a0d4c9-6afb-7711-a7b2-40459769110d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0d4c9-6afb-7711-a7b2-40459769110d","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-9-1\",\n  \"command\": \"task-board q 'get(TASK-260924-2zboyz){outcomeResources checklist status}' 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print(json.dumps(d, indent=1)[:6000])\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Get task outcome resources and checklist\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"{\\n \\\"checklist\\\": [\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Closed schemas Clone Read-Back Evidence Manifest 1.0.0 (pinned SPEC v0.7.0 10737+) and Clone Validation Report 1.0.0 (10755+): reflection-derived member census over every nested type, every member missing/extra/duplicated/miscased/wrong JSON type refused with a literal code at every entry; ids equal the JCS digest with only the id member omitted, recomputed independently in the test\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Semantic gates by whole-domain oracle: staged/live mode cannot be relabeled, expected and observed native IDs must be equal, sorted-unique evidence blobs, valid=true iff every applicable check passes (enumerate every combination of check outcomes x applicability), bounds at edge and edge+1\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Single owner per rule: every exported entry that accepts Fidelity Report, disposition/reason or Projection Plan data calls internal/clonefidelity / internal/cloneplan validators (AST call-graph census with control plant, structural guard against a second local implementation); axis inventory; importer outcome grid; task_delta, no registry edit\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Code written per task description and AC\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot \\\\u2014 never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio \\\\u2014 `n of m AC rows driven` \\\\u2014 and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant \\\\u2014 the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\\\",\\n   \\\"done\\\": true\\n  },\\n  {\\n   \\\"text\\\": \\\"A gate