{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c9bf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0d4c8-c91a-7382-bd41-b29e82ff449b"},"sequence":826,"recorded_at":1780531400001647,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"297f9a28-ff2a-4f3d-8e2c-f78b2b2814d6","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"297f9a28-ff2a-4f3d-8e2c-f78b2b2814d6","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"297f9a28-ff2a-4f3d-8e2c-f78b2b2814d6"},"call_id":"call_01a0d4ce564f74a1911639f35ac79bd3","text":"Read text file `internal/clonereadback/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TRACEABILITY — internal/clonereadback\n2|\n3|Fourth leaf of STORY-260830-21bxa3 (M4): Clone Read-Back Evidence\n4|Manifest 1.0.0 and Clone Validation Report 1.0.0 as closed schemas\n5|with JCS identities, pinned to SPEC v0.7.0 §13.14.2. The read-back\n6|mode derives from the trusted read authority threaded from the\n7|caller chain, and the report binds its references to the two\n8|trusted sibling reads. Tuple cross-match, plan/projected/fidelity\n9|pairing, and the Story registry belong to the final leaf\n10|(TASK-260830-1esv6u).\n11|\n12|Authority quotes below come from\n13|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` (pinned v0.7.0). Line numbers are\n14|1-based.\n15|\n16|## Axis inventory (written first)\n17|\n18|Every gate axis the conformance matrix walks, with its domain:\n19|\n20|| Axis | Domain | Oracle |\n21||---|---|---|\n22|| A1 shape members | every member of readback (16), evidence (5), report (23): reflection over the input types plus the sealed-minus-input envelope derivation | missing/extra/duplicated/miscased/wrong-type refused with the member literal at every entry, envelope included |\n23|| A2 schema/version | the two literal pairs from the registry (lines 170-171) | sibling URNs, 2.0.0/1.0 versions refused |\n24|| A3 read-back mode | staged\\|live (line 10739) | 2 closed modes seal under matching authorities + neighbors incl. invalid UTF-8 refused at Build, Decode, predicate |\n25|| A4 evidence kind | native_sample\\|parser_trace\\|marker_observation (lines 10748-10751) | 3 closed + 14 neighbors refused at Build, Decode, predicate |\n26|| A5 native-ID equality | equal vs unequal vs empty pairs | equal seals; unequal refuses (read-back) / decides valid=false (report) |\n27|| A6 valid rule | 2^7 check outcomes × ID eq/neq × 6 finding classes = 1536 combos | decided bit seals, flipped bit refuses, at Build and Decode |\n28|| A7 string bounds | [1..512] native IDs/heads, [1..128] media, chars not bytes | 0/1/512/513 and 127/128/129 ASCII + multibyte at edge |\n29|| A8 heads order | sorted unique [0..1024] | unsorted/dup/overlong refuse; 1024 admits, 1025 refuses, at Build and Decode |\n30|| A9 evidence order | sorted unique by (kind, blob) | 6 permutations admit 1; same-kind blob order; dup refuses |\n31|| A10 counts | evidence [0..65536], findings [0..4096] | 0/edge admit, edge+1 refuses at both entries |\n32|| A11 uint53/number | canonical integers, 2^53-1 max | 2^53, float, exponent, string, bool, null refuse |\n33|| A12 scalars | UUIDv7 operation, sha256 digests | v4/malformed refuse at Build; every sealed scalar member probed malformed at Decode |\n34|| A13 owner nesting | tuple/binding/findings documents | broken nested docs refuse with owner detail at every entry |\n35|| A14 extensions | reverse-DNS closed | open keys refuse at every entry |\n36|| A15 identity | JCS digest omitting only the self member | independent recompute agrees; other-member omission disagrees; tamper refuses; stale-id flip refuses under the flipped authority |\n37|| A16 UTF-8 | every Build-side string (7+4+9 derived fields) + heads + extensions | lone/trailing invalid bytes refuse with the member literal |\n38|| A17 ownership | 8 exports, 0 carrying fidelity/plan rows | row census empty; reachability to landed owners; no fork literals/selectors/imports |\n39|| A18 mode authority | purpose (3) × claimed mode (2) × entry (2), derived from ReadAuthority purpose (lines 3796-3797) | admit iff purpose maps to the claim; source_native and relabels refuse; resealed opposite mode refuses with a recomputing digest |\n40|| A19 read-ref binding | claims over {staged-id, live-id, unrelated}² × entry + missing + sibling relations | admit exactly (staged, live); equal/swapped/missing/twice-named/swapped-sibling refuse at both entries |\n41|\n42|## Clause map (spec sentence → gate → test)\n43|\n44|| # | Pinned clause | Gate | Production site | Test |\n45||---|---|---|---|---|\n46|| C1 | \"Clone Read-Back Evidence Manifest 1.0.0 contains exactly its schema/version\" + 15 members (10737-10747) | closed shape, 16 members | `DecodeReadBackEvidenceManifest`, `buildReadBackManifest` renders | `TestMemberCensus*` (readback/evidence) |\n47|| C2 | \"`read_back_evidence_manifest_id` under the omission rule\" (10738) | JCS identity | `Build…` seals, `verifySelfDigest` | `TestReadBackIdentityIndependent` |\n48|| C3 | \"`mode:staged\\|live`\" (10739) | closed mode | `ValidReadBackMode`, both entries | `TestModeVocabularyOracle` |\n49|| C4 | \"equal expected and observed native Session IDs\" (10741-10742) | equality | `checkNativeIdentityMatch`, both entries | `TestNativeIdentityEqualityOracle` |\n50|| C5 | \"`observed_environment:EnvironmentTuple`\" (10742) | owner tuple | `sessadapter.DecodeTuple` at both entries | `TestOwnerDelegation` |\n51|| C6 | \"`parsed_event_count:uint53`\" (10743) | uint53, no derivation (bound) | `checkUint53Bounds` / `> maxUint53` | `TestScalarGates`, `TestParsedCountAndStructuralDigestAreStatedBounds` |\n52|| C7 | \"`parsed_head_ids:sorted unique string[1..512][0..1024]`\" (10744) | sorted-unique | `checkSortedUniqueBoundedStrings` / environ | `TestParsedHeadIDsSweep` |\n53|| C8 | \"`workspace_binding:WorkspaceBinding`\" (10745) | owner binding | `clonebundle.DecodeWorkspaceBinding` | `TestOwnerDelegation` |\n54|| C9 | \"`structural_digest:digest`\" (10746) | digest, no derivation (bound) | `scalar.ParseDigest` / `checkDigest` | `TestScalarGates`, stated-bound test |\n55|| C10 | \"`evidence_objects:EvidenceObject[0..65536]`\" (10747) | count + row shape | `checkEvidenceCount`, row build/decode | `TestEvidenceCountEdges`, census |\n56|| C11 | \"`EvidenceObject` contains exactly…\" (10748-10751) | 5-member row, closed kind | `buildEvidenceObject`, `decodeEvidenceObject` | `TestMemberCensus*` (evidence), kind oracle |\n57|| C12 | \"Evidence rows are sorted unique by evidence kind/blob ID.\" (10752) | row order | `checkEvidenceOrder`, both entries | `TestEvidenceOrderSweep` |\n58|| C13 | \"Staged and live manifests are distinct and cannot be relabeled.\" (10753-10754) + \"Modes cannot be relabeled.\" (10580) + ReadAuthority purpose (3796-3797) | mode derived from trusted authority, claim must agree | `modeForAuthorityPurpose` + `checkModeAuthority`, both entries | `TestModeAuthorityGrid`, 4 relabel regressions, `TestModeRelabelRefused`, `TestModeBindsIdentity` |\n59|| C14 | \"`schema=urn:ax:schema:clone-validation-report`, `schema_version=1.0.0`\" (10756-10758) + 20 members (10758-10776) | closed shape, 23 members | `DecodeValidationReport`, `buildValidationReport` renders | `TestMemberCensus*` (report) |\n60|| C15 | \"`validation_report_id:digest` under the omission rule\" (10759) | JCS identity | `Build…` seals, `verifySelfDigest` | `TestReportIdentityIndependent` |\n61|| C16 | six manifest/fidelity digest refs + operation UUID (10760-10765) | staged/live refs bound to the trusted sibling reads; plan/projected/provider/fidelity stay opaque (reconciliation owns their pairing) | `checkReadRefs`, both entries + scalar gates | `TestReportReadRefRelationOracle`, equal/swap regressions, `TestScalarGates`, `TestDecodeScalarStrings` |\n62|| C17 | expected/observed IDs `string[1..512]` (10766-10767) | bounds; equality decides valid | bound gates + `decideValid` | string edges, valid oracle |\n63|| C18 | \"`target_environment:EnvironmentTuple`\" (10768) | owner tuple (cross-match is reconciliation) | `sessadapter.DecodeTuple` | `TestOwnerDelegation`, `TestReportTupleMatchIsReconciliationBound` |\n64|| C19 | seven check booleans (10769-10774) | required non-null booleans | `decodeValidationChecks` / Go bools | wrong-type census (null probe), oracle |\n65|| C20 | \"`findings:AdapterFinding[0..4096]`\" (10775) | owner findings + count | `sessadapter.DecodeFindings(·, 4096)` | `TestFindingsCountEdges`, delegation |\n66|| C21 | \"`valid=true` requires every boolean true, matching native IDs/tuple, and no error finding.\" (10776-10777) + \"every applicable check must pass\" (10582) | valid iff all-true ∧ IDs equal ∧ no error (tuple cross-match → reconciliation) | `decideValid` + `checkValidAgreement`, both entries | `TestValidWholeDomainOracle` (1536 combos) |\n67|| C22 | \"`extensions`\" on both shapes + registry URNs at 1.0.0 (170-171) | closed extensions, literal envelope | `clonebundle` extensions owner | `TestExtensionsClosed`, `TestEnvelopeLiterals` |\n68|\n69|Member-name derivation note: the pinned text states the\n70|read-back native-ID RULE (\"equal expected and observed native\n71|Session IDs\") without member names; the member names\n72|`expected/observed_target_native_session_id` follow the\n73|validation-report table (C17) and the read-back adapter success\n74|body (line 3843: `observed_target_native_session_id`), which spell\n75|both. The census exact-set test fails if production drifts from\n76|this spelling.\n77|\n78|## Gate × entry table\n79|\n80|Every production entry that reaches a gate is its own cell. B =\n81|Build refuses/admits, D = Decode refuses/admits, P = predicate.\n82|\n83|| Gate | BuildReadBack | DecodeReadBack | BuildReport | DecodeReport | Predicates |\n84||---|---|---|---|---|---|\n85|| closed members (A1) | renders exact¹ | refuses | renders exact¹ | refuses | — |\n86|| schema/version literals (A2) | renders | refuses | renders | refuses | — |\n87|| mode vocab (A3) | refuses | refuses | — | — | `ValidReadBackMode` |\n88|| evidence kind vocab (A4) | refuses | refuses | — | — | `ValidEvidenceKind` |\n89|| native-ID equality (A5) | refuses | refuses | decides | decides | — |\n90|| valid rule (A5/A6) | — | — | refuses flipped | refuses flipped | — |\n91|| string bounds chars (A7) | refuses | refuses | refuses | refuses | — |\n92|| heads order (A8) | refuses | refuses (owner) | — | — | — |\n93|| evidence order (A9) | refuses | refuses | — | — | — |\n94|| evidence count (A10) | refuses | refuses | — | — | — |\n95|| findings count (A10) | — | — | refuses (owner max) | refuses (owner max) | — |\n96|| uint53/number (A11) | refuses | refuses (owner type ceiling) | — | — | — |\n97|| scalars (A12) | refuses | refuses | refuses | refuses | — |\n98|| owner nesting (A13) | refuses w/ owner detail | refuses w/ owner detail | refuses w/ owner detail | refuses w/ owner detail | — |\n99|| extensions (A14) | refuses | refuses | refuses | refuses | — |\n100|| identity (A15) | computes | verifies | computes | verifies | — |\n101|| UTF-8 (A16) | refuses | n/a (JSON) | refuses | n/a (JSON) | predicates return false |\n102|| mode authority (A18) | refuses relabel/source | refuses relabel/source | — | — | — |\n103|| read-ref binding (A19) | — | — | refuses equal/swap/missing | refuses equal/swap/missing | — |\n104|\n105|¹ \"renders exact\" is pinned by `TestMemberCensusExactSets`\n106|(derived set vs sealed bytes), not by a refusal.\n107|\n108|## Mutant table (narrowing per gate, killed alone)\n109|\n110|Harness: `testdata/mutant_harness.py`. One raw log per plant per\n111|run carries the subprocess exit; the battery runs twice. All rows\n112|below are NARROWING (the gate stays present and admits exactly one\n113|forbidden member) except the marked control. No arm-deletes.\n114|\n115|| Mutant | Gate | Admits exactly | Killer (run alone) | Run1 | Run2 |\n116||---|---|---|---|---|---|\n117|| N-mode-archived | A3 | `archived` mode | `TestModeVocabularyOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n118|| N-kind-native | A4 | `native` kind | `TestEvidenceKindVocabularyOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n119|| N-identity-len | A5 read-back | same-length-differing IDs | `TestNativeIdentityEqualityOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n120|| N-valid-drop-staged | A6 | staged-false + valid=true | `TestValidWholeDomainOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n121|| N-valid-drop-live | A6 | live-false + valid=true | `TestValidWholeDomainOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n122|| N-valid-drop-marker | A6 | marker-false + valid=true | `TestValidWholeDomainOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n123|| N-valid-drop-identity | A6 | identity-false + valid=true | `TestValidWholeDomainOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n124|| N-valid-drop-binding | A6 | binding-false + valid=true | `TestValidWholeDomainOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n125|| N-valid-drop-resume | A6 | resume-false + valid=true | `TestValidWholeDomainOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n126|| N-valid-drop-generation | A6 | generation-false + valid=true | `TestValidWholeDomainOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n127|| N-valid-drop-ids | A6 | ID-mismatch + valid=true | `TestValidWholeDomainOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n128|| N-valid-drop-error | A6 | error finding + valid=true | `TestValidWholeDomainOracle` | KILLED | KILLED |\n129|| N-heads-dup | A8 Build | duplicated heads | `TestParsedHeadIDsSweep` | KILLED | KILLED |\n130|| N-evidence-dup | A9 | duplicated (kind, blob) | `TestEvidenceOrderSweep` | KILLED | KILLED |\n131|| N-evidence-count | A10 | 65537 rows, both entries | `TestEvidenceCountEdges` | KILLED | KILLED |\n132|| N-findings-count-build | A10 | 4097 findings at Build | `TestFindingsCountEdges` | KILLED | KILLED |\n133|| N-findings-count-decode | A10 | 4097 findings at Decode | `TestFindingsCountEdges` | KILLED | KILLED |\n134|| N-closed-readback | A1 | `zz_extra_member` in shape | `TestMemberCensusUnknownMissing` | KILLED | KILLED |\n135|| N-closed-evidence | A1 | `zz_extra_member` in row | `TestMemberCensusUnknownMissing` | KILLED | KILLED |\n136|| N-closed-report | A1 | `zz_extra_member` in shape | `TestMemberCensusUnknownMissing` | KILLED | KILLED |\n137|| N-schema-neighbor | A2 | sibling URN as schema | `TestEnvelopeLiterals` | KILLED | KILLED |\n138|| N-version-neighbor | A2 | `2.0.0` as version | `TestEnvelopeLiterals` | KILLED | KILLED |\n139|| N-relabel-admit | A15/C13 | docs valid under the other mode (now via the flipped-authority cell) | `TestModeRelabelRefused` | KILLED | KILLED |\n140|| N-parse-count-edge | A11 Build | 2^53 count | `TestScalarGates` | KILLED | KILLED |\n141|| N-mode-auth-build | A18 Build | cross-mode claims at Build | `TestBuildStagedAuthorityRefusesLiveClaim` | KILLED | KILLED |\n142|| N-mode-auth-decode | A18 Decode | resealed relabels at Decode | `TestDecodeStagedAuthorityRefusesResealedLiveClaim` | KILLED | KILLED |\n143|| N-purpose-source | A18 | source_native admitted as staged | `TestModeAuthorityGrid` | KILLED | KILLED |\n144|| N-report-refs-build | A19 Build | equal/swapped refs at Build | `TestBuildReportRefusesEqualReadRefs` | KILLED | KILLED |\n145|| N-report-refs-decode | A19 Decode | equal/swapped refs at Decode | `TestDecodeReportRefusesEqualReadRefs` | KILLED | KILLED |\n146|| N-envelope-alias | A1 | `Schema` normalized before closure | `TestMemberCensusMiscased` | KILLED | KILLED |\n147|| N-utf8-lone | A16 | lone-invalid bytes at Build strings | `TestBuildUTF8Reflection` | KILLED | KILLED |\n148|| N-media-bound-build | A7 Build | 129-char media at Build | `TestMediaTypeStringEdges` | KILLED | KILLED |\n149|| N-media-bound-decode | A7 Decode | 129-char media at Decode | `TestMediaTypeStringEdges` | KILLED | KILLED |\n150|| N-heads-item-build | A8 Build | 513-char heads at Build | `TestParsedHeadIDsSweep` | KILLED | KILLED |\n151|| N-heads-count-build | A8 Build | 1025 heads at Build | `TestParsedHeadIDsSweep` | KILLED | KILLED |\n152|| N-heads-item-decode | A8 Decode | 513-char heads at Decode | `TestParsedHeadIDsSweep` | KILLED | KILLED |\n153|| N-heads-count-decode | A8 Decode | 1025 heads at Decode | `TestParsedHeadIDsSweep` | KILLED | KILLED |\n154|| N-scalar-digest-build | A12 Build | `not-a-digest` at Build | `TestScalarGates` | KILLED | KILLED |\n155|| N-scalar-digest-decode | A12 Decode | `not-a-digest` at Decode | `TestDecodeScalarStrings` | KILLED | KILLED |\n156|| N-uuid-build | A12 Build | `not-a-uuid` at Build | `TestScalarGates` | KILLED | KILLED |\n157|| N-uuid-decode | A12 Decode | `not-a-uuid` at Decode | `TestDecodeScalarStrings` | KILLED | KILLED |\n158|| N-control-neutral | control | nothing (comment-only) | full suite | SURVIVED | SURVIVED |\n159|| P-census-entry | A17 plant | ninth export carrying a row | `TestExportedAPIInventory` | RED | RED |\n160|| P-owner-call-removed | A17 plant | (removed owner call) | `TestOwnerReachability` | RED¹ | RED¹ |\n161|| P-forked-literal | A17 plant | re-added owner literal | `TestNoForkedLiterals` | RED | RED |\n162|| P-severity-second | A17 plant | second Severity matcher | `TestErrorSeverityDecidedOnDecodedField` | RED | RED |\n163|| P-guard-literal-list | A1 plant | 10-name literal list | `TestMemberCensusNoLiteralList` | RED | RED |\n164|\n165|¹ red via build failure (the removed call leaves the variable\n166|undefined): the pin depends on the call's presence.\n167|\n168|Kill-mechanism honesty: N-closed-*, N-schema-neighbor, and\n169|N-version-neighbor admit past the weakened gate and are then\n170|refused downstream by the identity gate; the killer fails on the\n171|changed refusal literal, which proves the weakened gate's presence\n172|and literal for the admitted member. N-valid-drop-* disagree with\n173|the spec-derived oracle (never with production), which is the kill.\n174|N-mode-auth-* and N-report-refs-* are conjunct drops at one call\n175|site (the N-valid-drop shape): the killed admission is direct, and\n176|the same mutants also redden the twin regression, the driving\n177|oracle, and the `TestOwnerReachability` pin, which is the expected\n178|same-gate collateral. N-utf8-lone is killed by the literal shift\n179|at `ExpectedTargetNativeSession` (the downstream equality refusal\n180|lacks the member literal) and would admit at `media_type`; the\n181|vocab oracles redden under it for the same literal shift.\n182|N-session-bound was WITHDRAWN after it survived the first battery:\n183|a single-member bound widening is masked by the sibling bound gate\n184|under the equality constraint; the edge is proven by\n185|`TestNativeSessionStringEdges` and the conjoining gate by\n186|N-identity-len. N-uint53-decode was WITHDRAWN after it survived\n187|this revision's first battery: the environ owner runs its uint53\n188|type check before the call-site max, so no local widening can\n189|admit 2^53 at Decode; behavior is pinned by `TestScalarGates`\n190|and the Build-side ceiling by N-parse-count-edge. Both\n191|withdrawn logs ride the evidence tar under `withdrawn/`.\n192|\n193|## Importer outcome grid\n194|\n195|This leaf adds `internal/clonereadback` (new files only) and edits\n196|no landed file: the tracked tree equals the story tip (`5e40826`\n197|= trunk `6d3bff9` + the three signed story checkpoints), so the\n198|five reused owner packages are byte-identical between base and\n199|candidate and their suites are green on the candidate tree — no\n200|input class moved. The grid is keyed (package, entry, input).\n201|Base is the story tip; candidate is the uncommitted tree. The\n202|read-back entries consume `sessadapter.ReadAuthority` values and\n203|the report entries consume validated `ReadBackManifest` siblings;\n204|no new owner call is added — `DecodeReadAuthority` runs in the\n205|tests to mint genuinely validated fixtures, mirroring the caller\n206|chain.\n207|\n208|| Package | Entry | Input classes through this leaf | Base | Candidate | Moved |\n209||---|---|---|---|---|---|\n210|| `internal/environ` | `DecodeStrictObject` | valid objects; dup-member / trailing-data / non-object docs | green | green | none |\n211|| `internal/environ` | `StringLength` | ASCII + multibyte at every bound | green | green | none |\n212|| `internal/environ` | `CheckStringBounds` | in-bound; over-max / under-min / non-string | green | green | none |\n213|| `internal/environ` | `CheckUint53Bounds` | in-bound; fraction / exponent / string / 2^53 | green | green | none |\n214|| `internal/environ` | `CheckDigest` | valid sha256; malformed | green | green | none |\n215|| `internal/environ` | `CheckUUIDv7` | valid v7; v4 / malformed | green | green | none |\n216|| `internal/environ` | `CheckSortedUniqueStrings` | sorted-unique; unsorted / dup / over-count | green | green | none |\n217|| `internal/scalar` | `ParseDigest` / `ParseUUIDv7` | valid; malformed | green | green | none |\n218|| `internal/scalar` | `SHA256Digest` | canonical omit-self bytes | green | green | none |\n219|| `internal/canonicaljson` | `Canonicalize` | manifest / report / row objects | green | green | none |\n220|| `internal/clonebundle` | `EncodeExtensions` | closed maps; bad keys / values | green | green | none |\n221|| `internal/clonebundle` | `CheckExtensionsClosed` | closed; open / nested-dup | green | green | none |\n222|| `internal/clonebundle` | `OmitSelfDigest` | member maps + self field; tampered claims | green | green | none |\n223|| `internal/clonebundle` | `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` | valid bindings; broken bindings | green | green | none |\n224|| `internal/sessadapter` | `DecodeTuple` | valid tuples; broken tuples | green | green | none |\n225|| `internal/sessadapter` | `DecodeFindings` | valid arrays; broken rows / over-count | green | green | none |\n226|| `internal/clonereadback` | `BuildReadBackEvidenceManifest` | (input, authority): valid manifest; every invalid class in the clause map incl. relabel/source | n/a (new) | green | none (new surface, no importer yet) |\n227|| `internal/clonereadback` | `DecodeReadBackEvidenceManifest` | (bytes, authority): sealed manifest; mutated / hand-built / resealed docs | n/a (new) | green | none |\n228|| `internal/clonereadback` | `BuildValidationReport` | (input, staged, live): valid report; every invalid class incl. flipped valid and ref relations | n/a (new) | green | none |\n229|| `internal/clonereadback` | `DecodeValidationReport` | (bytes, staged, live): sealed report; mutated / hand-built docs | n/a (new) | green | none |\n230|| `internal/clonereadback` | 4 vocabulary helpers | in-vocabulary; neighbors incl. invalid UTF-8 | n/a (new) | green | none |\n231|\n232|No `internal/clonefidelity` or `internal/cloneplan` row: no entry\n233|carries their row shapes (references are digests), pinned by\n234|`TestOwnerRowCensusIsEmpty` + `TestNoOwnerImports`.\n235|\n236|## Stated bounds (sibling scope or spec-silent, not waived)\n237|\n238|- Report \"matching tuple\" needs the read manifests' observed\n239|  tuples as cross-inputs; only the single-tuple shape is gated\n240|  here. Owned by the final reconciliation leaf.\n241|- Plan/projected/provider/fidelity pairing across shapes needs\n242|  the wider reconciliation inputs; those digests stay opaque here\n243|  (the staged/live read binding against the trusted siblings IS\n244|  gated here). Final leaf.\n245|- Report/operation coherence across the three shapes (the reads'\n246|  operation vs the report's) is a cross-input pairing; ungated\n247|  here. Final leaf.\n248|- `parsed_event_count` carries no stated derivation from heads or\n249|  rows; any uint53 admits. Spec-silent.\n250|- `structural_digest` carries no stated preimage; any digest\n251|  admits. Spec-silent.\n252|- Blob descriptor agreement (descriptor vs blob ID + byte count)\n253|  needs an object store; these entries take no fetch. Unverified\n254|  here by construction.\n255|- `parsed_event_count` vs `parsed_head_ids` cardinality: no stated\n256|  relation; independent bounds only.\n257|- Authority freshness/expiry: the entries consume the Purpose of\n258|  an already-validated authority the caller chain mints; expiry\n259|  enforcement lives where the chain mints it. Composition bound.\n260|- Owner-inner rules (tuple/binding/finding inner members,\n261|  extension value model, decode-side uint53 type ceiling) are\n262|  delegated to the sessadapter/clonebundle/environ suites; the\n263|  wiring is pinned by the delegation table and the reachability\n264|  census, and a narrowing inside those owners belongs to their\n265|  packages, not to a fork here. Excluded from the measured\n266|  narrowing ratio.\n267|- Single-member native-ID bound narrowings are masked by the\n268|  sibling bound under the equality constraint (see mutant table);\n269|  edges proven directly. Excluded from the measured ratio.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
