512/513 edges are proven\\ndirectly at both entries of both shapes, ASCII + multibyte.\\n² The decode-side uint53 ceiling is the environ owner's type\\ncheck, which runs before the call-site max (withdrawn row\\nN-uint53-decode, log preserved); behavior pinned by\\n`TestScalarGates`, Build ceiling by N-parse-count-edge.\\n\\n## Whole-domain counts\\n\\n- valid oracle: 128 check combos × 2 ID relations × 6 finding\\n  classes = 1536 combinations, each through Build-seal,\\n  Build-flipped-refusal, Decode-seal, Decode-flipped-refusal.\\n- mode-authority grid: 3 purposes × 2 modes × 2 entries = 12\\n  cells + 4 invalid-purpose cells; every Decode mismatch cell\\n  first proves the sealed id recomputes.\\n- read-ref relation oracle: 7 claim pairs + 2 missing + 3\\n  sibling relations = 12 cells × 2 entries.\\n- mode oracle: 2 closed + 19 neighbors (Build/Decode/predicate).\\n- kind oracle: 3 closed + 14 neighbors (Build/Decode/predicate).\\n- member census: 16 + 5 + 23 derived members (reflection +\\n  sealed-envelope derivation) × missing/extra/miscased/6-wrong-\\n  types/duplicated at the decode entries.\\n- scalar strings: 5 + 2 + 8 value-classified members ×\\n  malformed probes at the decode entries.\\n- UTF-8: 20 derived string fields × 3 poisons at the Build\\n  entries + heads + extensions.\\n\\n## Reviewer rework guards (epic rejection patterns)\\n\\n- (a) circular expectations: every refusal asserts a literal\\n  member/code fragment from the pinned text at the production\\n  entry; no `got == pkg.Constant` assertions.\\n- (b) helper vs entry: shared gates (`checkNativeIdentityMatch`,\\n  `checkEvidenceOrder`, `checkValidAgreement`/`decideValid`,\\n  `checkModeAuthority`/`modeForAuthorityPurpose`,\\n  `checkReadRefs`) are AST-pinned reachable from BOTH sibling\\n  entries; narrowings kill through the entries, one per entry\\n  path for the authority and ref gates.\\n- (c) forked gates: authority decode, tuple/binding/findings,\\n  strict-object/measure/uint53/digest/extension/identity all\\n  delegate to landed owners; the purpose→mode binding and the\\n  ref→sibling binding are this leaf's rules (no owner exports\\n  them); structural tests pin zero fork literals/selectors/\\n  imports.\\n- (d) census vs behavior: every census has a behavioral twin\\n  (unknown-member docs refused, flipped bits refused, resealed\\n  relabels refused, swapped refs refused, broken nested docs\\n  refused with owner detail).\\n- (e) mutant honesty: narrowings only (no arm-deletes), one raw\\n  log per plant per run with subprocess exits, applied neutral\\n  control SURVIVED, two masked rows withdrawn with logs\\n  preserved, kill mechanisms audited (no compile-error kills).\\n- (f) prose vs tests: \\\"reaches the owner\\\" = AST reachability +\\n  delegation refusals; \\\"no second implementation\\\" = literal,\\n  selector, import, and decider pins; \\\"derives the mode\\\" =\\n  purpose grid + resealed-relabel refusals with recomputing ids;\\n  bounds stated where the spec is silent or ownership delegates\\n  (count/digest derivations, tuple cross-match, descriptor\\n  agreement, owner-inner rules, authority freshness).\\n...\\n100\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5897,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1475,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
